From: Akashic <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:33:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support Angelica 2.2.24+ font API (GL texture ids)

Angelica 2.2.24 (GTNewHorizons/Angelica#2165) changed
BatchingFontRenderer.pushDrawCmd and FontProvider.getTexture from a
ResourceLocation to a GL texture id. With Angelica 2.2.24 or newer the
BatchingFontRendererMixin shadow is not found, the required mixin config
fails, BatchingFontRenderer never loads and the client crashes with
NoClassDefFoundError in the FontRenderer constructor. The glyph and modern
font providers would also throw AbstractMethodError.

- BatchingFontRendererMixin: shadow and redirect pushDrawCmd(IIIZ)V;
  the handler checks texture != 0 instead of != null.
- AngelicaGlyphProvider / AngelicaModernFontProvider: getTexture returns
  the texture's GL id (AngelicaFontCompat.textureId). Only NecroTempus'
  own pushDrawCmd redirect sees it, so a texture that is not uploaded yet
  returns -1 instead of being loaded.
- AngelicaFontApiProbe: the Angelica mixin is applied only when the
  installed Angelica has this API (read from the class file, nothing is
  loaded), so an older Angelica no longer crashes the client.
- Compile against Angelica 2.2.37.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
